diff --git a/docs/API.md b/docs/API.md
index 71adb5bd..82a9c1d6 100644
--- a/docs/API.md
+++ b/docs/API.md
@@ -185,6 +185,41 @@ The response is a JSON object with fields:
 * `errorCode`: string, optional, machine-readable description of the error. Possible values: `ACCOUNT_DOES_NOT_EXIST`, `UNKNOWN_OPER_CLASS`, `INVALID_VHOST`, `FEATURE_DISABLED`, `UNKNOWN_ERROR`.
 * `error`: string, optional, human-readable description of the failure
 
+`/v1/channel_access`
+--------------------
+
+This endpoint syncs a channel's invite-only mode and its account invite exceptions (`+I a:<account>`, see "account extbans" in the manual). It never creates a channel. The request is a JSON object with fields:
+
+* `channel`: string, name of the channel
+* `inviteOnly`: boolean, optional: set (`true`) or clear (`false`) `+i`. Omit it to leave `+i` alone.
+* `registeredOnly`: boolean, optional: the same for `+R`
+* `accounts`: list of strings, the accounts that must have an `a:<account>` entry on the `+I` list
+* `setBy`: string, optional (default `API`), recorded as the creator of the entries it adds. Existing `a:` entries with this creator whose account is not in `accounts` are removed; entries anyone else added are never touched.
+
+Changes are announced to the channel's members as `MODE` lines from the server and saved with the channel's registration (an unregistered channel loses them when it empties). The response is a JSON object with fields:
+
+* `success`: boolean, whether the request succeeded (`true` for a channel that doesn't exist)
+* `exists`: boolean, whether the channel exists; if false, nothing was changed
+* `registered`: boolean, whether the channel is registered
+* `added`, `removed`: lists of strings, the casefolded accounts whose entries were added and removed
+* `inviteOnly`, `registeredOnly`: booleans, whether the channel is now `+i` / `+R`
+
+`/v1/sajoin`
+------------
+
+This endpoint joins every connected client of an account to channels, with the same semantics as `SAJOIN` (channel modes and bans don't apply; a channel that doesn't exist is created). An always-on client with no attached session is not joined. The request is a JSON object with fields:
+
+* `accountName`: string, name of the account
+* `channels`: list of strings, the channels to join
+
+The response is a JSON object with fields:
+
+* `success`: boolean, whether the request succeeded (`true` with `clients` 0 if nobody is logged into the account)
+* `clients`: number, how many connected clients of the account were joined
+* `joined`: list of strings, the channels every client is now in
+* `failed`: object, maps each channel that couldn't be joined to the reason
+* `errorCode`: string, optional: `ACCOUNT_DOES_NOT_EXIST` for an invalid account name
+
 `/v1/ns/saregister`
 -------------------
 
