+++ b/docs/MANUAL.md
@@ -869,6 +869,10 @@ This means that **bob** will be able to join even without being `/INVITE`'d.
 
 For everything else, this mode acts like the `+b - Ban` mode.
 
+#### Account extbans
+
+`+b`, `+e` and `+I` entries of the form `a:<account>` match clients logged into that account, whatever their nick, username or host (`EXTBAN=,am` in `RPL_ISUPPORT`). For example, `/MODE #test +I a:bob` lets anyone logged into the account **bob** join `#test` while it is `+i`. Account names are matched exactly (no wildcards).
+
 ### +k - Key
 
 This channel mode lets you set a 'key' that other people will need to join your channel. To set a key:
